    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThe Wildings is a deceptively spacious three-bedroom detached residence extending to approximately 194.74 sq. m. (2,107 sq. ft.), set on a private 0.26 hectare site in the coastal setting of Doughmore Doonbeg.Ideally positioned just 200 metres off the Wild Atlantic Way route, the property is approximately 300 metres from Doughmore Beach and Trump International Golf Links & Hotel, while Doonbeg village is just 2.7km away.Built in 2006 with a B energy rating, this spacious home comprises an entrance hallway, reception room, open-plan kitchen/dining area, utility, bathroom and ground-floor bedroom, with two en-suite bedrooms upstairs. A detached building to the rear offers ample extra storage and has planning permission for a gym and home office.Electric gates with cut-stone pillars lead to a wraparound gravel driveway, lawned areas and natural boundaries. The property has oil-fired central heating, mains water and a bio-cycle treatment system, with full planning permission to extend to a five-bedroom home (plans available on request).The location is ideal for a permanent or holiday home, with Doughmore Beach, the Wild Atlantic Way and excellent golf all close by. Doonbeg village provides all the essential services and amenities for day-to-day living. The Wildings presents an excellent opportunity in a highly attractive West Clare coastal setting with viewing strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL 002295."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 7.3m x 2.3m\nTile flooring, decorative ceiling coving with two centre rose features, wall mounted light fitting, decorative radiator cover, carpeted timber railed stairs leading to first floor landing with ample space for understair storage, doors to main reception, kitchen dining and bedroom one.\n\nMain Reception - 5.2m x 4.6m\nTimber style flooring, two front aspect windows, decorative ceiling coving with centre rose feature, solid fuel insert with timber surround, tv point and double doors leading to kitchen dining.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 8.2m x 4m\nKitchen Area - Tile flooring, built-in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, integrated wicker baskets, eye level glass display units, tile splash back, integrated appliances including dishwasher, gas hob, extractor hood and fan, double oven, one and a half bowl sink, fridge freezer, decorative ceiling coving, breakfast island and open access to dining area.Dining Area - Tile flooring, side aspect window, full length glass sliding door to the rear and decorative ceiling coving.\n\nUtility Room - 3.55m x 2.55m\nTile flooring, rear door access, solid timber wall and base units, integrated spot lighting, integrated sink, plumbing for washing machine and dryer and space for fridge (Note - these three white goods items will part of the sale price)\n\nGround Floor Bathroom - 3.7m x 2m\nFully tiled ceiling to floor, decorative ceiling coving, low level wc, wash hand basin with fitted mirror and overhead light, bath unit and separate corner shower with pump shower and glass shower door.\n\nGround Floor Bedroom One - 4.65m x 4.55m\nTimber flooring, dual aspect windows to the front and side, buit-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and storage and decorative ceiling coving with centre rose feature.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 4.9m x 2.5m\nCarpeted flooring, door to hotpress housing immersion tank and shelving, storage into the eves, doors to bedroom two and three.\n\nBedroom Two En-Suite - 6.5m x 4.45m\n*Size includes en-suiteTimber flooring, velux window to the front, alcove window to the rear, wall to wall built-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and storage and door to en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite - \nFully tiled ceiling to floor, velux window, low level wc, wash hand basin, corner fitted shower unit with pump shower and glass shower door.\n\nBedroom Three En-Suite - 6.5m x 4.65m\nTimber flooring, velux window to the front, closed off area to the rear with window, built-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and storage and door to en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite - 2m x 1.8m\nTile flooring, low level wc, wash hand basin and corner fitted shower with electric shower and glass shower door.\n\nDetached Home Office - 8.7m x 5.05m\nGlass sliding door to the front, PVC door to the side, concrete floors, fully wired, split into two sections by stud partition.Front Section - Pull down stira stairs leading to overhead storage that is fully floored.Rear Section - Has separate wc and wash hand basin.\n\nOutside - \nFront - Electric wrough iron gates, cut stone pillars, lawn area, wraparound gravel drive way, concrete slab area to the side of shed. Rear - Lawn area, natural boundaries.\n\n"
      },
